Confirmed. Line 150 `LocalDate from = activation.periodStart != null ? activation.periodStart : evalDate` — the `false` arm is **dead code**: `challengeBases` reaches this line only after `!activation.isActiveOn(evalDate)` is false, and `FidelityActivation.isActiveOn` returns `false` whenever `periodStart == null`. So `periodStart` is provably non-null here; the `evalDate` arm is unreachable and cannot be covered without touching `src/main` (out of scope).

## Report — `CardContextBuilderTest`

**Branch count:** 29/30 covered (96%). Instructions 227/228 (99%).

**Justified residue (1 branch):** `CardContextBuilder.java:150`, the `else` arm of `periodStart != null ? periodStart : evalDate`. Unreachable: the enclosing guard `ruleCode == null || !isActiveOn(evalDate)` already `continue`s for every activation with a null `periodStart` (`FidelityActivation.isActiveOn` returns `false` on null `periodStart`), so control never reaches line 150 with `periodStart == null`. Covering it would require weakening the guard in `src/main` — out of scope.

**Coverage map (18 tests, all green):**
- `countVisits`: projection adds current visit / doesn't when today already recorded / ingestion counts only recorded (verifies the today-probe is never issued) — the `!countCurrentVisit` both arms and both `?0:1` arms.
- `aggregateByCommunity`: found rule with code, unknown rule (null ternary arm), rule without community code (`communityCode==null` arm), two rules merged (covers `BigDecimal::add`).
- `activeMembershipCodes`: coded membership collected, null community (leg 1 false), code-less community (leg 2 false).
- `challengeBases`: active challenge computes base from `periodStart` (true ternary arm + arg verify); each `||` leg — null ruleCode, inactive activation, unknown rule, non-challenge rule.
- `build`: month-border straddle at 2026-01-31T23:59 vs 2026-02-01T00:00 (evalDate derivation and clock/finder wiring verified on both sides, §30.3/§25.1); full carry of account, global earn, per-rule cumulative and instant into the context.

**Determinism (§24.6):** `ProgramClock` is mocked and the fiscal instant is fixed via the `evaluationDateTime` parameter — no real clock, no `now()`. Month-boundary behavior is tested with the two instants straddling the border, not the campaign day.

**Architecture:** plain unit — no `@QuarkusTest`, no H2. All six domain static finders intercepted with `mockStatic` in try-with-resources; entity instances built in memory so `isActiveOn`/`communityCodeFromSpec` run for real. No `mockConstruction` needed (the builder persists nothing). BigDecimals asserted by `compareTo`; assertions from `org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions` only.

**Files read:** `CardContextBuilder`, `CardContext`, `ProgramClock`, `FidelityActivation`, `FidelityMembership`, `FidelityRule`; signature-grepped `FidelityMovement`/`EarnTrace`/`EarnTraceLine`/`FidelityAccount`/`FidelityCommunity`/`BaseEntity`; existing `AmountEvaluationTest` for house style.

**Iterations:** 1 (green on first run; JaCoCo confirmed the single dead-branch residue).

