## Report

**Class under test:** `com.intermarche.fidelity.earn.ValuationReader` (pure reconciliation reader — no clock, so no `DateTimeProvider` involved; the temporal-boundary rule doesn't apply).

**Result:** 18 tests, all passing.

**Branch coverage (JaCoCo):** **90/92 branches = 97 %**, instructions **506/506 = 100 %**.

**Justified residue (2/92):** line 212, `prorata(...)` — the `weight == null` and `total == null` legs of the §31.2 null-guard `weight == null || total == null || total.signum() == 0`. `prorata` is `private static` with a single caller, `reallocateDiscount`, which passes `item.amount != null ? item.amount.ttc() : BigDecimal.ZERO` for `weight` (never null) and an accumulator seeded at `BigDecimal.ZERO` and only `.add`-ed for `total` (never null). Both legs are unreachable defensive guards; reaching them would require reflection to bypass the public API. The third leg (`total.signum() == 0`, zero denominator) **is** covered, along with its non-zero counterpart.

**Notable branches exercised:**
- `read`: null response; the two-leg `offer == null || offer.amount == null` skip; `items` null-vs-non-null ternary; empty-items verify skip; `item == null || item.lineId == null` skip; `consuming` true/false via `isStandard` (Standard prefix / other prefix / null type); `advantage == null` / `!isDiscount` / real-discount legs; `totalPrice` null-vs-non-null; global reconciliation `>0` at the centime boundary (pass at 0.01, throw at 0.05); unknown-EAN warning raised once with `containsKey` short-circuit; known-EAN no warning.
- `verifyOfferInvariant`: `>0` throw and one-centime-tolerance pass; `item != null && item.amount != null` all legs.
- `reallocateDiscount`: pro-rata split with last-line remainder, `targets.isEmpty()` no-op, target-collection legs (null offer / null type / non-match / match-with-null-items), `acc == null` continue (discount on a dropped-offer line), zero-denominator split.
- `LineAccumulator.addTranche`: null and non-null `amount` / `produceEan` / `quantity`.

Every `BigDecimal` asserted via `compareTo`; amounts checked to the centime (e.g. HT pro-rata `13.34`/`6.66` with remainder). Only `Product.findByEan` mocked, via `mockStatic(Product.class)` in try-with-resources.

