## Report — `com.intermarche.fidelity.batch.BatchService`

**Result:** new test class `BatchServiceTest`, 9 tests, all green.

**Branch coverage (JaCoCo):** **34 / 35 branches = 97%** (instructions 342/344). One justified residue.

**Justified residue — 1 branch, `BatchService.java:178`:**
```java
return residualOld.signum() < 0 ? BigDecimal.ZERO : residualOld;
```
The `< 0` **true** arm is **unreachable**. In `residualUpToYear`, each iteration computes `residual = credit − min(debits, credit)`, which is always ≥ 0 (it is `0` when `credit ≤ debits`, else `credit − debits > 0`). `residualOld` is a running sum of those non-negative residuals, so it can never be negative for any input — the guard is a §31.2-style protective clamp with no reachable input. Covered the **false** arm; the true arm is documented residue, not a coverage gap.

**Branches covered (both arms / each leg):**
- `run`: all 3 `switch` arms (EXPIRY/PURGE/ACTIVATION_VOID); `!dryRun` record guard both arms (dry-run skips `recordRun`, execution builds+persists `BatchRunLog`).
- `expiry`: `dryRun ? candidate : lock` both arms; `residual.min(available)` both directions (residual-taken 15<20, available-taken 1<3); `toExpire.signum() <= 0` both arms (skip when available=0); `!dryRun` post guard both arms.
- `residualUpToYear`: `debits.min(credit)` both directions in one FIFO walk (debits=12 → full consume of 2024, partial of 2025); `entry.getKey() <= expireYear` both arms (2024/2025 included, 2026 excluded); ternary false arm.
- `purge` & `activationVoid`: `dryRun ? candidate : lock` both; `!dryRun` both; `balance.signum() > 0` both (positive posts, negative/zero skips); `balance.max(ZERO)` both (positive kept, negative clamped to 0).

**Method/§ compliance:** time only via mocked `ProgramClock` frozen at `NOW=2026-03-01T09:00` (§24.6); `earnYear` border probed by included 2025 / excluded 2026 (§30.3); Panache statics via `mockStatic` in try-with-resources — inherited `list` stubbed on its declaring class `PanacheEntityBase`, entity finders on their own classes; `BatchRunLog.persist()` neutralised with `mockConstruction`; accounts are mocks; every `BigDecimal` asserted by `compareTo` at scale 2; English + full Javadoc, no blank lines in method bodies, JUnit assertions only.

