## Report — `CardNumberGeneratorTest`

**Result:** 8 tests, all passing. `verify` clean.

**Branch coverage: 17/18 (94%)** · Instructions 152/157 (96%). One justified residue (below).

**Branches enumerated & covered**
- `digitsOnly` — `value == null` **true** (null setting value) and **false** arms; `digits.isEmpty()` **true** (all-letters `"ABC"` → default) and **false** (`"7A7"` → `"77"`) arms.
- `base12` — `body.length() > 12` **true** (16-digit prefix → last-12 truncation) and **false** (padding path); the `for (i < fill)` loop entered (fill > 0) and exited.
- `checkDigit` — `i % 2 == 0` ternary both arms (even/odd indices of every 12-digit base); outer `% 10` driven to **0** (sum multiple of ten → check digit `0`, card `2990000000040`) and to non-zero.
- `generate()` loop — `findByCardNumber(...) == null` **true** arm (free number returned) and **false** arm (collision → walk forward to the next sequence); loop-exit + `IllegalStateException` throw (every candidate taken → 1 000 000 iterations exhaust the bound).

All card numbers asserted as absolute 13-digit literals (EAN-13 check digits pre-computed and cross-checked).

**Justified residue — 1 branch, `CardNumberGenerator.java:69`**
`return padded.length() > 12 ? padded.substring(0, 12) : padded.toString();` — the **true arm is unreachable**. This ternary is only reached in the `else` of `body.length() > 12`, i.e. when `prefix.length() + seq.length() <= 12`; there `padded` is built as `prefix + (12 - prefix.length() - seq.length()) zeros + seq`, whose length is **exactly 12**, so `padded.length() > 12` is always false. It's dead defensive code that cannot be driven from `generate()` without altering `src/main` — left untouched per scope.

**Architecture:** plain unit — no `@QuarkusTest`, no H2, no clock (the class has no temporal logic, so no `DateTimeProvider`). Panache finders (`find`, `count`) and the setting reader are mocked through `PanacheEntityBase` in try-with-resources `mockStatic`; each `PanacheQuery` is built before the stub chain to avoid nested-stubbing.

**Files read:** `CardNumberGenerator.java` (target); `FidelityProgramSetting.java` and `FidelityAccount.java` (excerpts — static-finder signatures, `value` field); `AppUserTest.java` / `FidelityMembershipTest.java` (bench pattern).

**Iterations:** 3 — (1) ambiguous varargs `find` overload → disambiguated with `(Object) any()`; (2) `UnfinishedStubbing` from building mocked queries inside `thenReturn(...)` → hoisted query construction into helpers; (3) same on the throw test → hoisted → green.

No `src/main` change; only the test class was touched.
