All 5 tests pass and the build is green. The JaCoCo report shows **5/6 branches (83%)** with a single uncovered branch on the `} catch (Exception e) {` line.

I investigated that residue: it is the well-known **try-with-resources synthetic branch** — javac desugars `try (InputStream in = …)` into a close handler containing `if (primaryExc != null) { try { in.close(); } catch (Throwable t) { primaryExc.addSuppressed(t); } }`. The uncovered leg requires `in.close()` to itself throw *while the body is already unwinding*. Since `in` comes from `getClass().getResourceAsStream(...)` (a real classpath stream that cannot be substituted without touching `src/main`, which is out of scope), that leg is unreachable. The two *reachable* legs — normal completion and body-throws-then-close-succeeds — are both covered by `loadAppliesImporterForExistingResource` and `loadSwallowsImporterException`.

