## Report — `PasswordResetService`

**Branches: 18/18 (100%).** Lines 15/15 methods; instructions 96% (168/175).

**Tests: 12, all green.** Verify (JaCoCo) BUILD SUCCESS.

### Branches covered
- `requestReset` — `user == null` short-circuit (nothing deleted/stored/mailed) **and** the full send path (pending tokens invalidated, hashed token persisted with `now().plusMinutes(ttl)` expiry, mail subject/recipient/label/username/TTL/link asserted).
- `trimTrailingSlash` (private, via the mailed link) — all four legs: null base, blank non-null base (`"   "`), trailing-slash base (trimmed, no `//`), slash-less base (verbatim).
- `resetPassword` — `token == null` leg, `token.isBlank()` leg, valid token; `reset == null` leg, `!isUsableAt(now)` leg, usable token; `policyError != null` (weak password) **and** `== null` (success).
- Success path asserts `setPassword`, `mustChangePassword` cleared, `usedAt == FIXED`, both `persist()` calls; `validatePassword` runs for real.

### Time
`DateTimeProvider` fixed to `FIXED = 2026-08-08T10:00` per test, cleared after. Token expiry asserted as `FIXED.plusMinutes(30)`; usability verified against `isUsableAt(FIXED)` — never the campaign clock (§24.6, §30.3).

